    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve for \\( x \\) in the equation \\(\\log_x 4 = \\log_{27} 3\\), we can use the change of base formula for logarithms. The change of base formula states that \\(\\log_a b = \\frac{\\log_c b}{\\log_c a}\\) for any positive \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) where \\(a \\neq 1\\) and \\(c \\neq 1\\).\n\nFirst, we use the change of base formula to express \\(\\log_{27} 3\\) in terms of base 10 or base \\(e\\). However, a simpler approach is to use the fact that \\(\\log_3 27 = 3\\) because \\(27 = 3^3\\). Therefore, we can rewrite the equation as:\n\\[\n\\log_x 4 = \\log_{27} 3 = 3\n\\]\nThis means that \\(x^3 = 4\\). To find \\(x\\), we take the cube root of both sides of the equation:\n\\[\nx = \\sqrt[3]{4}\n\\]\nThus, the solution is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\sqrt[3]{4}}\n\\]",
